From d3f7407fbf98e103787eb93aaba8b96478adee0c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Allen <cma@bitemyapp.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 01:36:47 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] input/keyboard: Keep the layout in `set_modifier_state`

`set_modifier_state` passed `layout_effective & STATE_LAYOUT_*` as the
depressed, latched and locked layouts to `update_mask`. `layout_effective`
is a layout index and the `STATE_LAYOUT_*` constants are state component
flags (16, 32 and 64), so all three were 0 for any of the first 16 layouts,
and each call switched the keyboard back to its first layout.

`ModifiersState` doesn't select a layout, so pass the state's current
layout components through unchanged.

Found in Aizome, whose per-keyboard keymaps restore Caps Lock and Num
Lock with `set_modifier_state` and had to set the layout again after it.
The new test sets the second layout of a "us,de" keymap, sets Caps Lock,
and checks the layout; it fails without this change.

Developed with AI assistance (Claude Code).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
